      "intent_anchors": [
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA1",
          "statement": "Keep the front face flat and free of recesses or raised bezels so that the textured surface remains continuous and hides scuffs; the display window must be flush with the surrounding face.",
          "category": "form",
          "must_preserve": true
        },
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA2",
          "statement": "Maintain a two-part shell with a single horizontal split line on the back or bottom, no visible screws on the front or top, and no extra parts beyond the two mouldings and the printed logo.",
          "category": "cost",
          "must_preserve": true
        },
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA3",
          "statement": "Use rABS with a light texture (VDI 24-27) and a dark warm grey colour to hide fingerprints and scuffs, and protect the front face from gloss variation.",
          "category": "cmf",
          "must_preserve": true
        },
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA4",
          "statement": "Place the intake grille on the top face as a simple slot pattern that can be moulded with a single straight-pull tool; no side actions or lifters for the intake.",
          "category": "cost",
          "must_preserve": true
        },
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA5",
          "statement": "Design the USB-C opening on the bottom face with a simple rectangular cut-out and a wall thickness around it of at least 1.2 mm to survive repeated plugging; no additional reinforcement parts.",
          "category": "durability",
          "must_preserve": true
        }
      ],
      "rationale": "This concept adapts the approved reference desk unit into a slimmer, more slab-like form suited to the monolith_slab direction. The envelope is reduced slightly in width and height to save material and cost while staying within the 125 x 75 x 30 mm limit. The chamfered slab silhouette with 8 mm corner radii is familiar to tooling, uses a simple two-part shell, and avoids undercuts. The front face is kept plain with only a flush display window; the intake is moved to the top face as a moulded slot pattern that requires no side actions, and the USB-C port is on the bottom edge for easy cable routing. rABS with a light texture and dark warm grey colour meets the brief's scuff-hiding and cost priorities; the printed logo is the only decoration. The design avoids extra parts, secondary operations beyond pad printing, and complex tooling, targeting the CNY 12 housing cost at 10k units/year."
    },
